    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d7">

                <pb facs="0100" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg26"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1104.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 6, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In accordance with the desire expressed in
                    your despatch No. 1579, of the 4th of November, I presented a copy of the same
                    to Lord Clarendon, who freely expressed his approbation of it, after which I
                    concluded to give it publicity through the press. It accordingly appeared
                    simultaneously in all the London morning papers of Saturday last, the 2d
                    instant. I transmit a copy of the Times of that day, and likewise a copy of the
                    same paper of the 5th, containing <pb facs="0101" n="27" xml:id="pg27"/> a
                    leader on the subject. The tone of this is conciliatory until towards the close,
                    when allusions are made of an ambiguous character.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d7-a1.xml" xpointer="d7-a1"/>
            </div>
